      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That sense of purpose being extinguished is a heavy, suffocating darkness, and you're right, platitudes about \"finding meaning\" feel hollow when the core of you feels gone. What you're describing is a genuine, deep-seated grief for the person you used to be, and that grief is valid. Instead of trying to force a future, maybe you can just focus on the immediate, small moments of existing, without the pressure of what comes next. Be gentle with yourself while you navigate this immense void.",
      "source": "target",
